  "term": "spermatogenesis",
  "definition": "Spermatogenesis is the process by which male germ cells develop into sperm. In the source described here, this involves a gradual change from a round cell into an elongated sperm cell as the acrosome forms, the cytoplasm shifts toward the head, and the flagellum develops.",
